  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Four identical plates each of area $a$ are separated by a distance $d$. The connection is shown below. what is the capacitance between $P$ and $Q ?$ <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2013_phy_q41.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wG1nM",
      "text": "$2 a \\varepsilon_{0} / d$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "jkE0c",
      "text": "$a \\varepsilon_{0} /(2 d)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6cykP",
      "text": "$a \\varepsilon_{0} / d$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "irQGb",
      "text": "$4 a \\varepsilon_{0} / d$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Suppose the pair of plates is connected to positive terminal of the battery and the pair of plates $Q$ is connected to the negative terminal of the battery. <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2013_phy_a41.png\">\r\n\r\nFrom figure, it is clear that we have two capacitors $C_{1}$ and $C_{2}$. Positive plates of $C_{1}$ are connected to positive plate of $C_{2}$ and negative plate to negative. Therefore $C_{1}$ and $C_{2}$ are in parallel.\r\nSo, $\\quad C_{p}=C_{1}+C_{2}=2 C=\\frac{2 \\varepsilon_{0} a}{d}$",
    "image": null
  },
